  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dog wearing a Native American headdress",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the dog wearing the headdress, which serves as a stand-in for a Native American person in the meme's racist trope. The user identifies with or imagines themselves as the recipient of the 'free blanket' (a symbol of colonial coercion), thereby projecting their own perspective onto the dog's role in the meme's narrative. This projection is implicit, as there are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the meme's structure invites the user to identify with the dog as the subject of the colonial 'gift' and the 'grateful' recipient.",
